# The bundled Azure DevOps live folder loads in the app next to GitHub, GitLab and Jira: its plug-in
# describes itself in the sandboxed host, its icon resolves, and "New Azure DevOps Live Folder" is a
# command the bar finds (#542). What the plug-in asks Azure DevOps and how it reads the answers is
# LiveFolderProviderTests.azureDevOps.
# promise: #542
budget rss=900
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}

wait 2
cra://commandbar?query=azure devops
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarRows=azure
expect-log Cra command bar rows azure: open=1 .*New Azure DevOps Live Folder
